<Wiki
  title="Existing project"
  description="Import a Composer project into puv.toml and install the locked graph."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>Existing project</h1>
  <p>
    A directory that already has <code>composer.json</code> does not start with
    <a href="/wiki/commands/init"><code>init</code></a>. Import it, then install the graph.
  </p>
  <pre class="block">puv contain
puv sync</pre>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/contain"><code>puv contain</code></a> moves <code>require</code> and
      <code>require-dev</code> into <code>puv.toml</code>. A present <code>composer.lock</code> is
      copied and not resolved again. A missing lock is resolved from <code>composer.json</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/wiki/commands/sync"><code>puv sync</code></a> installs exactly that lock. It does
      not resolve.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Plain shell scripts are copied. PHP callables, <code>@composer</code> calls, and plugin events
    are skipped with a warning. The Composer files stay until
    <code>puv contain --clean</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    After that, everyday work is the same as a
    <a href="/wiki/new-project">new project</a>: <a href="/wiki/commands/add"><code>add</code></a>,
    <a href="/wiki/commands/run"><code>run</code></a>,
    <a href="/wiki/commands/check"><code>check</code></a>. What the import will not copy is
    <a href="/wiki/scope">scope</a>.
  </p>
</Wiki>
